  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food Security and Rural Development - Mali</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Local structures are set up and trained to cope with the negative effects of climate change/environmental/natural shocks. They will learn about mitigation and adaption to the negative effects of climate change and finally will apply improved biological and mechanical measures (contingency and risk plans, stockage, assisted natural regeneration of land, composting, improved techniques). Focus is given to those in most vulnerable situations, such as women headed households, pregnant, lactating and women of childbearing age, children and youth, and people living with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
